From db08d4c6d74e45f052984a8b5d408850f326a917 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: uuu <3100141307@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:31:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Verify PE/COFF header construction in linux-bzimage
 builder

Verify all eight handwritten pe_header functions under explicit setup ELF
layout preconditions. Specify exact section fields, aligned layout arithmetic,
optional-header fields, and the ordered 368-byte header representation.

Retain the original nested helper, callback, runtime assertions, arithmetic,
and serialization loop. Use the project verified bitflags macro to expose
bitwise contracts; fixed-width operands and flag methods preserve the original
masks. Enable proc_macro_hygiene for the native loop contract attribute.

Centralize audited xmas-elf, bytemuck and little-endian integer contracts in
vstd_extra::external and pin the modeled dependency versions. ELF parsing,
object representation, external derives and the existing mapping assumptions
remain trusted; field-level packed byte encodings are not proved.

Validation:
- cargo dv verify -p linux-bzimage-builder --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
  (152 verified, 0 errors)
- cargo dv build -p linux-bzimage-builder --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
- make (ostd: 1558 verified, 0 errors)
- cargo dv fmt -p linux-bzimage-builder vstd_extra
- git diff --check
- Differential execution: 512 valid layouts produce identical complete PE
  bytes; 4 malformed layouts produce matching panics.
